# Non-Goals (SR-App)

Detailed reference: `docs/steering/foundation/non-goals.md`. Anything here is OUT unless a
decision-log entry explicitly reverses it (reversal is an architectural decision).

**SR-App is NOT (in MVP):**
- A public customer portal / booking site / marketplace — internal tool only.
- Real-time fleet **telematics** (no OBD/engine data, live vehicle GPS, background/continuous GPS trails).
- A full **accounting** system (no GL, tax filing, payroll, A/R aging automation) — invoices + payment recording only.
- A **native** app — it is a PWA; offline is limited and explicit.
- A **payment processor** — we record payments; no card capture/gateway in MVP.
- **Multi-tenant** SaaS — single company.
- A **routing/optimization** engine — dispatch assigns manually.
- A full **HR/scheduling** suite — time tracking is per-job labor, not payroll.
- An **offline-first CRDT** app — offline covers a narrow write set only.

**Failure modes:** sneaking telematics/accounting/gateway complexity under a feature name; implying
background location a PWA can't guarantee.

**Escalation:** reversing any non-goal REQUIRES a decision-log entry before implementation.
